  ------------------------------------------------------------
    the programme
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      0:00  I · SKILL SHOT — BALL 1
            Right-hand shooter alley; a helical steel coil
            spring compresses behind the brass plunger tip
            and launches the mirror-chrome silverball around
            the top arch through three rollover star lanes.

      0:14  II · POP BUMPERS — 1000 PTS
            The ball drops into a triangle of cyan, magenta
            and solar-amber mushroom pop bumpers whose skirts
            kick down and fire concentric shockwaves on every
            solenoid chime strike.

      0:34  III · DROP TARGETS — LOCK LIT
            Twin rubber-ringed flippers snap up to bank the
            silverball into a five-bank of drop targets,
            knocking them flat one by one before climbing the
            elevated four-rail chrome wireform skyway.

      0:55  IV · JACKPOT MULTIBALL
            Three mirror-chrome silverballs erupt across
            extruded 3D neon acrylic prisms and graze each
            other in mid-air inside the wireform ring.

      1:18  V · PLUMB BOB — DANGER
            The cabinet shudders sideways; inside the dark
            mahogany cabinet, the swinging conical brass
            plumb-bob slams into the circular contact ring
            with a high-voltage blue-white electric arc.

      1:29  VI · TILT — GAME OVER
            All playfield inserts go dark under the crimson
            TILT backglass reflection; the flippers go limp,
            and the lone silverball rolls silently between
            them into the outhole drain.

  ------------------------------------------------------------
    how to run
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      Double-click intro.html in Edge or Chrome on Windows
      10 or 11, wait for the orange neon bar, then click.
      No server, no flags. ESC leaves fullscreen. A discrete
      GPU is recommended. Tested on an RTX 5090.

